<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grafschaft Bentheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grafschaft Bentheim is a district in the south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> border, with Nordhorn as its seat. It corresponds largely to the former County of Bentheim, which passed to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> in 1815 and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1866. The area is known for Bentheim sandstone and close ties with the neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, and many of its people belong to the Reformed Church.</p></div>
